<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n3271" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ăquātĭlis</span></b> ,
		e, adj.
		id.. <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I. A..</b>
			<i>Living</i>, <i>growing</i>, or <i>found</i>, <i>in</i> or <i>near water</i>, <i>aquatic</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">vescimur bestiis et terrenis et aquatilibus et
					volantibus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cic. N. D. 2, 60, 151</span></i>
			 B. and K.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>B.</b>
			<i>Subst.</i>: <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ăquātĭlĭa</span></b> ,
				ium, n., <i>aquatic
				animals</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">aquatilium in medicinā beneficia,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plin.
					31, 1, 1, § 1</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>Having a watery taste</i>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὑδαρής</span>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">sunt amari absinthi, aquatiles cucumeris,
					cucurbitae, lactucae,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plin.
					19, 12, 61, § 186</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>III.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ăquātĭlĭa</span></b> ,
				ium, n., <i>a disease of
				cattle</i>, <i>watery vesicles</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">hydatides,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Veg. Vet. 2, 49</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
